  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Second Thoughts & Wide Angle Enz (Enzyclopedia Volumes One & Two Appendices)\" is a definitive 2LP vinyl release from Split Enz's acclaimed Enzyclopedia series, pairing the remastered original mix of the band's 1976 album Second Thoughts—handled by Phil Kinrade from the original tapes—with a bonus LP of Wide Angle Enz, featuring rare live recordings and archival rough mixes. Originally recorded in London with Roxy Music guitarist Phil Manzanera producing, Second Thoughts reworks much of the material from their 1975 debut Mental Notes, delivering an eccentric art rock statement filled with theatrical flair, prog-rock experimentation, and quirky New Zealand pop sensibilities penned by co-founders Tim Finn and Phil Judd. Tracks like \"Late Last Night,\" \"Sweet Dreams,\" and \"Stranger Than Fiction\" showcase the band's angular rhythms, vivid songcraft, and penchant for dramatic arrangements, marking their international debut in Europe and North America (where it was retitled Mental Notes with altered artwork).\n\nThe Wide Angle Enz companion disc adds significant value, blending Eddie Rayner-remixed live cuts from a December 1975 performance at Melbourne's Reefer Cabaret (including \"Sweet Dreams,\" \"Stranger Than Fiction,\" and \"129 (Matinee Idyll)\") with vault rarities like rough mixes of \"Late Last Night\" and an exclusive unreleased \"archival rough mix\" of early single \"Matinee Idyll (129).\" This appendices set builds on the Enzyclopedia box's contents—previously limited to remixed Second Thoughts and retooled Beginning—offering fans pristine audio of the unaltered 1976 mix alongside period-specific ephemera that captures Split Enz's raw, evolving energy during their early Antipodean-to-global transition. Released on Chrysalis, it underscores the band's rock foundations while highlighting their innovative, makeup-clad art rock legacy and enduring cult appeal.",
      "generated_at": "2026-03-11T13:19:13.046722",
      "model": "sonar",
      "source": "perplexity"
    }
